der: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">testMode: false</code> â†’ it's genuinely in live mode</span></li><li class="text-sm flex items-start gap-2" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));"><span class="text-blue-400 mt-0.5">â€¢</span><span><code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">liveBlocked: false</code> â†’ live charging is not blocked</span></li><li class="text-sm flex items-start gap-2" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));"><span class="text-blue-400 mt-0.5">â€¢</span><span><code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">credentialSource: "saved"</code></span></li><li class="text-sm flex items-start gap-2" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));"><span class="text-blue-400 mt-0.5">â€¢</span><span>The build/typecheck passes with no errors.</span></li></ul><div class="h-2"></div><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));">So the source code and the saved keys are all correct â€” the only gap is that your published app hasn't been rebuilt with that code.</p><div class="h-2"></div><h3 class="iqx-markdown-heading" data-level="2">What to do after republishing</h3><div class="h-2"></div><ul class="space-y-1 my-2 ml-4"><li class="text-sm flex items-start gap-2" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));"><span class="text-blue-400 mt-0.5">â€¢</span><span><strong class="font-semibold" style="color: var(--studio-text, #0f172a);">Republish / deploy</strong> the app so production gets the live-mode code.</span></li><li class="text-sm flex items-start gap-2" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));"><span class="text-blue-400 mt-0.5">â€¢</span><span><strong class="font-semibold" style="color: var(--studio-text, #0f172a);">Re-enter the keys in production</strong> (Admin â†’ Payment gateway) if your published app uses a <strong class="font-semibold" style="color: var(--studio-text, #0f172a);">separate database</strong> from the preview â€” the encrypted keys live in the database, so they don't automatically move to a different DB. (If it shares the preview DB, they're already there.)</span></li><li class="text-sm flex items-start gap-2" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));"><span class="text-blue-400 mt-0.5">â€¢</span><span><strong class="font-semibold" style="color: var(--studio-text, #0f172a);">Register the production webhook URL</strong> in Paystack (<code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">https://&lt;your-production-domain&gt;/api/payments/webhook</code>), not the preview URL. The admin page shows the exact URL to use.</span></li><li class="text-sm flex items-start gap-2" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));"><span class="text-blue-400 mt-0.5">â€¢</span><span><strong class="font-semibold" style="color: var(--studio-text, #0f172a);">Confirm on production</strong>: open <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">https://&lt;your-production-domain&gt;/api/health</code> â€” it should show <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">testMode: false</code> and <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">liveBlocked: false</code>.</span></li></ul><div class="h-2"></div><h3 class="iqx-markdown-heading" data-level="2">One thing to double-check on the keys themselves</h3><div class="h-2"></div><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));">The form's <strong class="font-semibold" style="color: var(--studio-text, #0f172a);">"Paystack Webhook Secret"</strong> field is for the <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">whsec_â€¦</code> secret (Paystack â†’ Settings â†’ API Keys &amp; Webhooks) â€” <strong class="font-semibold" style="color: var(--studio-text, #0f172a);">not</strong> the webhook URL. The webhook <em style="color: rgb(56, 189, 248);">URL</em> is what you paste into Paystack's dashboard. If these got swapped, the webhook signature check would fail; note that the payment would still credit via the redirect â†’ server-side verification path, but it's worth confirming the secret is the <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">whsec_â€¦</code> value.</p><div class="h-2"></div><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));">Also: this applies to the <strong class="font-semibold" style="color: var(--studio-text, #0f172a);">admin-page (saved) path only</strong>. If you instead set the live keys via environment variables, you must <em style="color: rgb(56, 189, 248);">also</em> set <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">PAYSTACK_ALLOW_LIVE=true</code> â€” that's the deliberate opt-in for env-var live keys. The saved/admin-page path doesn't need it.</p><div class="h-2"></div><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--studio-text-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.72));">Republish first, then check the production <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">/api/health</code> output â€” if <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">testMode</code> still isn't <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono" style="background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--studio-panel-soft, rgba(15,23,42,0.06)) 70%, transparent 30%); color: rgb(14, 165, 233); border: 1px solid var(--studio-border, rgba(148,163,184,0.25));">false</code> there, tell me what it returns and I'll dig further.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="response-footer-shell"><div class="flex items-center gap-1 response-footer-actions "><button type="button" class="studio-metrics-trigger w-7 h-7 rounded-[8px] flex items-center justify-center transition-all" aria-label="Good response"><svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" width="24" height="24" viewB